WEBVTT

00:00:06.565 --> 00:00:09.045
Why did we drive
all the way across town

00:00:09.125 --> 00:00:10.925
for The Happy Platter?

00:00:11.085 --> 00:00:14.365
We'd like a booth over there,
near the philodendron.

00:00:14.525 --> 00:00:16.645
Good, right?
Near the philodendron.

00:00:16.725 --> 00:00:18.565
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

00:00:19.165 --> 00:00:21.965
This platter doesn't look
all that happy to me.

00:00:22.165 --> 00:00:24.045
It looks bored.

00:00:24.125 --> 00:00:26.085
Ha-ha! The Bored Platter!

00:00:26.245 --> 00:00:28.445
I thought Vi would want
a change of pace

00:00:28.525 --> 00:00:29.605
from drive-in food.

00:00:29.765 --> 00:00:31.485
I like drive-in food.

00:00:31.645 --> 00:00:33.405
Does this mean vegetables?

00:00:33.565 --> 00:00:35.405
A balanced diet
means vegetables, kiddo.

00:00:35.565 --> 00:00:36.965
Get used to it.

00:00:37.765 --> 00:00:39.045
TONY: Good evening, everyone.

00:00:39.805 --> 00:00:41.565
-BOB: Oh, no!
-(COUGHING)

00:00:41.765 --> 00:00:42.965
-Is she all right?
-Violet, are you okay?

00:00:43.125 --> 00:00:44.165
(COUGHING)
Nothing to see here.

00:00:44.245 --> 00:00:45.245
Yeah, more napkins
would be good.

00:00:45.325 --> 00:00:46.885
-I'm fine, I'm fine.
-It happens all the time here.

00:00:47.045 --> 00:00:48.125
Mops it right up.

00:00:48.285 --> 00:00:50.805
Normally, she doesn't
ever drip like this.

00:00:50.965 --> 00:00:53.085
-Would you like water, sir?
-BOB: Yes.

00:00:53.245 --> 00:00:56.005
Yes, I would.
This is my daughter...

00:00:56.165 --> 00:00:57.565
-who you must know, right?
-God. Stop.

00:00:57.725 --> 00:00:58.845
-Hello.
-Violet.

00:00:59.005 --> 00:01:00.205
Hello, Violet.

00:01:00.285 --> 00:01:01.405
(BOB CHUCKLING)

00:01:01.485 --> 00:01:02.725
Hey, Vi, say hi to...

00:01:02.885 --> 00:01:04.285
Don't push it, Dad.

00:01:04.445 --> 00:01:06.085
I'm Dash, her little brother.

00:01:06.245 --> 00:01:07.245
Hello.

00:01:07.325 --> 00:01:09.805
Mmm. This is
really good water.

00:01:09.885 --> 00:01:10.965
It's very refreshing.

00:01:11.125 --> 00:01:12.245
Spring water, is it?

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:14.845
I don't know, sir.
I think it's tap.

00:01:15.005 --> 00:01:16.445
Well, it is very good.

00:01:16.605 --> 00:01:17.845
Excellent tap.

00:01:18.005 --> 00:01:19.405
Excuse me.

00:01:20.205 --> 00:01:22.045
Well, nice to meet you.

00:01:22.205 --> 00:01:23.645
-Where'd she go?
-DASH: Mmm.

00:01:23.805 --> 00:01:25.805
To find a good place
to be angry?

00:01:26.965 --> 00:01:29.645
Tonight, we go now to
a special remote interview...

00:01:29.805 --> 00:01:30.845
with Elastigirl.

00:01:31.005 --> 00:01:32.085
ELASTIGIRL:
How you feeling, Chad?

00:01:32.165 --> 00:01:33.165
You doing all right?

00:01:33.245 --> 00:01:35.645
I'm fine.
The doctors checked me out.

00:01:35.805 --> 00:01:37.685
(STAMMERS) I have no memory
of the event.

00:01:37.805 --> 00:01:39.565
I gotta tell you,
it's pretty strange

00:01:39.645 --> 00:01:40.645
to see a recording...

00:01:40.845 --> 00:01:43.565
of yourself the night before
and have no recollection.

00:01:43.725 --> 00:01:45.445
I don't think
anyone needs to worry.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:47.605
We've taken many precautions
tonight though.

00:01:47.765 --> 00:01:49.085
Where are you right now?

00:01:49.245 --> 00:01:52.205
On a case, in a secure
undisclosed location.

00:01:52.365 --> 00:01:53.685
CHAD: I wanna talk
about you...

00:01:53.885 --> 00:01:56.325
starting with your save
of a runaway train.

00:01:56.485 --> 00:01:58.765
Here's an exclusive
unedited clip

00:01:58.845 --> 00:02:00.085
from your own suit cam.

00:02:00.245 --> 00:02:01.445
Roll the clip.

00:02:01.845 --> 00:02:03.125
ELASTIGIRL: This thing's
really moving.

00:02:04.285 --> 00:02:06.765
100 and climbing.
How much track is built?

00:02:06.925 --> 00:02:08.405
EVELYN: About 25 miles.

00:02:10.045 --> 00:02:12.965
SCREENSLAVER: The Screenslaver
interrupts this program...

00:02:13.125 --> 00:02:14.365
for an important announcement.

00:02:14.565 --> 00:02:16.405
I'll be damned. She knew.

00:02:16.565 --> 00:02:18.085
Let's see
if your gadget works.

00:02:18.285 --> 00:02:20.285
Don't bother
watching the rest.

00:02:20.445 --> 00:02:21.125
Gotcha!

00:02:21.325 --> 00:02:23.765
Elastigirl doesn't
save the day.

00:02:24.285 --> 00:02:26.885
She only postpones her defeat.

00:02:27.085 --> 00:02:29.245
And while she postpones
her defeat...

00:02:29.405 --> 00:02:32.685
you eat chips and watch
her confront problems...

00:02:32.845 --> 00:02:35.125
that you are too lazy
to deal with.

00:02:35.285 --> 00:02:37.965
Superheroes are part
of your brainless desire...

00:02:38.125 --> 00:02:40.645
to replace true experience
with simulation.

00:02:41.485 --> 00:02:44.485
You don't talk,
you watch talk shows.

00:02:44.965 --> 00:02:47.885
You don't play games,
you watch game shows.

00:02:48.365 --> 00:02:50.885
Travel, relationships, risk...

00:02:51.725 --> 00:02:54.485
every meaningful experience
must be packaged...

00:02:54.645 --> 00:02:57.445
and delivered to you
to watch at a distance.

00:02:57.965 --> 00:03:00.285
So that you can remain
ever sheltered...

00:03:00.445 --> 00:03:01.445
ever passive...

00:03:02.205 --> 00:03:04.685
ever ravenous consumers...

00:03:04.845 --> 00:03:07.365
who can't bring themselves
to rise from their couches...

00:03:07.845 --> 00:03:11.205
break a sweat
and participate in life.

00:03:11.965 --> 00:03:14.045
You want superheroes
to protect you...

00:03:14.845 --> 00:03:18.725
and make yourselves ever more
powerless in the process.

00:03:19.045 --> 00:03:21.645
While you tell yourselves
you're being looked after.

00:03:22.565 --> 00:03:24.445
That your interests
are being served.

00:03:24.845 --> 00:03:27.405
And your rights
are being upheld.

00:03:27.565 --> 00:03:30.405
So that the system can
keep stealing from you...

00:03:30.605 --> 00:03:33.405
smiling at you all the while.

00:03:33.605 --> 00:03:36.965
Go ahead,
send your Supers to stop me.

00:03:37.125 --> 00:03:39.325
Grab your snacks,
watch your screens,

00:03:39.445 --> 00:03:41.445
and see what happens.

00:03:41.605 --> 00:03:44.485
You are no longer in control.

00:03:44.645 --> 00:03:46.005
I am.

00:04:11.885 --> 00:04:13.885
(MACHINES BEEPING)

00:04:49.645 --> 00:04:51.205
(CLOCK CHIMING)

00:05:27.805 --> 00:05:29.365
SCREENSLAVER: Find anything?

00:05:30.045 --> 00:05:31.325
(GROANING)

00:05:36.525 --> 00:05:38.445
(YELLING)

00:05:41.805 --> 00:05:43.445
(BOTH GRUNTING)

